        "chars_per_1k_ink": 13.6
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        180,
        287,
        2038,
        521
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "1) The employee must not be asked to waive any of his constitutional rights. One of the reasons the dismissals were invalidated in *Gardner* and *Sanitationmen* is that the employees were asked to waive their rights to immunity against criminal prosecution.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.4112,
          "min": -2.0787
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
          "mean": -0.3466,
          "min": -0.6932
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 53,
          "mean": -0.0137,
          "min": -0.429
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 11090,
        "area_px": 406315,
        "density": 0.02729,
        "chars": 257,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 23.17
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        180,
        566,
        2087,
        803
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "2) At the commencement of the disciplinary proceeding, the employee must be given the warning set forth on pp. 1-2 of this memorandum, even if he has previously announced his intention not to testify in his own behalf, and even if he is charged only with incompetence.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.3493,
          "min": -1.9046
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0002
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 56,
          "mean": -0.0012,
          "min": -0.0557
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 9258,
        "area_px": 424942,
        "density": 0.02179,
        "chars": 268,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 28.95
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        180,
        846,
        2062,
        962
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "3) The hearing must be formally and carefully conducted and an exact stenographic or other record kept.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 19,
          "mean": -0.3166,
          "min": -1.9294
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.0157,
          "min": -0.3154
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 1894,
        "area_px": 205101,
        "density": 0.00923,
        "chars": 103,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 54.38
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        180,
        985,
        2087,
        1590
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "4) The employee must be given an opportunity to explain why he failed or refused to answer questions at the inquiry, or failed to appear, if such failure to appear or answer is the basis of the charges against him. He need not be asked the original questions again, although he may be. If the employee offers, at the disciplinary hearing, to answer the original inquiry questions, he should be allowed to do so. His willingness to answer the original questions at this subsequent proceeding does not necessarily eliminate the charge based on refusing to answer or appear at the inquiry. The extent and value of the employee's cooperation at the disciplinary hearing, however, should be taken into consideration in determining the nature and extent of the discipline, if any, to be imposed.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.2178,
          "min": -1.8097
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 150,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0025
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 17461,
        "area_px": 1077468,
        "density": 0.01621,
        "chars": 789,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 45.19
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        257,
        1617,
        2097,
        1861
      ],
      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "5) No charge against an employee for failure to answer questions should mention Section 1123 of the Charter. This section has been declared unconstitutional and should not be used as the basis of any action. Any reference to Article I, Section 6 of the New York State Constitution would also be inappropriate.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.3316,
          "min": -1.6966
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 2,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0002
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 62,
          "mean": -0.0004,
          "min": -0.0167
        }
      },
